# libmpv core DLLs — too large for GitHub (>100 MB).
# Download from https://github.com/zhongfly/mpv-winbuild/releases
# and place next to libmpv-wrapper.dll before building.
libmpv-2.dll
mpv.dll
mpv-2.dll
mpv-1.dll

# Bundled ffmpeg (~80 MB) — removes the system-PATH requirement for
# the silence/black skip detectors. Drop a static ffmpeg.exe here
# (e.g. from https://www.gyan.dev/ffmpeg/builds/ — ffmpeg-release-
# essentials) before building; tauri.conf.json's resources glob
# ("lib/**/*") bundles it and silencedetect.rs::ffmpeg_bin prefers
# it over PATH. Absent → falls back to PATH ffmpeg (no regression).
ffmpeg.exe

# Bundled ffprobe — the Phase-4 cast transmux prerequisite (cast/
# transcode.rs probes the source's codecs to decide copy-vs-reencode).
# Ships from the SAME ffmpeg build above (ffprobe.exe sits next to
# ffmpeg.exe in those archives). Absent → casting falls back to
# direct-play only (cast_ffmpeg_present() returns false; MKV won't
# transmux for Chromecast). DLNA TVs decode MKV natively regardless.
ffprobe.exe

# yt-dlp (~18 MB) — resolves a "Watch Trailer" YouTube id to a direct CDN URL
# for in-player trailer playback (trailer.rs::resolve_trailer_url). On-demand
# runtime dep: hosted on the runtime-deps prerelease + downloaded on first use,
# so it's never bundled. Drop the matching build here for `tauri dev`; the SHA
# in runtime_deps.rs must match the asset uploaded to the prerelease.
yt-dlp.exe
